estimates of PASP was 8.0 mm Hg with 95% limits of agreement ranging from -28.4 to 44.4 mm Hg. CONCLUSIONS DE estimates 
of PASP are inaccurate in patients with PH and should not be relied on to make the diagnosis of PH or to follow the     
efficacy of therapy."}, {"study_index": 23, "title": "Recommendations for cardiac chamber quantification by             
